feed:
{{ config.title }} - Writing
{{ writing.description }}


Zola
{#- WARNING: derive the feed timestamp from the newest entry, not from Zola's
    last_updated. This feed is scoped to the writing section, while last_updated
    is site-wide — a change anywhere else would move the feed's  without
    any entry having changed, which tells readers to refetch for nothing.

    WHY a full scan instead of `sort(attribute="date") | last` (typikon#92,
    ported from 4f8c1531 -> b61228cb): the feed's  must be the most
    recent EDIT across every entry, and one entry's most recent edit is
    `updated` when set, `date` otherwise. Sorting by `date` alone and then
    reading THAT entry's `updated` misses an older-dated entry whose own
    `updated` is more recent than the newest-dated entry's own — exactly the
    case  exists to surface. set_global (not set) is required so an
    assignment inside the for loop survives past that iteration;
    date(format="%s") | int turns each value into an epoch integer because
    Tera's `>` only compares numbers, never date/string values directly. -#}
{%- if pages | length > 0 -%}
{%- set_global feed_updated_ts = 0 -%}
{%- set_global feed_updated = "" -%}
{%- for p in pages -%}
{%- set p_updated = p.updated | default(value=p.date) -%}
{%- set p_ts = p_updated | date(format="%s") | int -%}
{%- if p_ts > feed_updated_ts -%}
{%- set_global feed_updated_ts = p_ts -%}
{%- set_global feed_updated = p_updated -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set feed_updated = last_updated | default(value=now()) -%}
{%- endif %}
{{ feed_updated | date(format="%+") }}
{{ feed_url | safe }}
{{ author_name }}{{ author_uri | safe }}
{%- for page in pages %}

  {{ page.title }}
  {{ page.date | date(format="%+") }}
  {{ page.updated | default(value=page.date) | date(format="%+") }}
  {{ page.extra.author | default(value=author_name) }}

  {{ page.permalink | safe }}
  {{ page.description }}
  {{ page.content }}

{%- endfor %}
